file=Behavioural Science/frame/operational/principles/frame-principles.md · f·p:frame \· principles=> Universal-only.\n\n1. **Facts unchanged across frames.** Frame changes = OK; fact changes = manipulation.\n2. **Every alternative frame ethics-tagged.**\n3. **Predictions cite mechanism** (prospect theory / temporal discounting / narrative structure).\n4. **Curse-of-knowledge check mandatory** on longer narratives.\n5. **Facts first, structure second.**\n6. **One dimension per A/B variant** — no confounds.\n7. **Sample size from Shared OS**, never invented.\n8. **Guardrail metric on every A/B test** — local win with global loss = defect.\n9. **Every claim traces to source.**\n10. **Verification-before-completion inherited.**\n